{"id":"heart","name":"Heart","aliases":["Heart"],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:heart","torrey:heart-the"],"groups":["The Unregenerate","Instances Of Hardened Hearts","Change Of","Instances Of"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Heart","text":"According to the Bible, the heart is the centre not only of spiritual activity, but of all the operations of human life. “Heart” and “soul” are often used interchangeably (Deut. 6:5; 26:16; comp. Matt. 22:37; Mark 12:30, 33), but this is not generally the case. The heart is the “home of the personal life,” and hence a man is designated, according to his heart, wise (1 Kings 3:12, etc.), pure (Ps. 24:4; Matt. 5:8, etc.), upright and righteous (Gen. 20:5, 6; Ps. 11:2; 78:72), pious and good (Luke 8:15), etc. In these and such passages the word “soul” could not be substituted for “heart.” The heart is also the seat of the conscience (Rom. 2:15). It is naturally wicked (Gen. 8:21), and hence it contaminates the whole life and character (Matt. 12:34; 15:18; comp. Eccl. 8:11; Ps. 73:7). Hence the heart must be changed, regenerated (Ezek. 36:26; 11:19; Ps. 51:10-14), before a man can willingly …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G2588","lemma":"καρδία","xlit":"kardía","gloss":"the heart","kjv":"heart","count":48,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H3824","lemma":"לֵבָב","xlit":"lêbâb","gloss":"the heart","kjv":"bethink themselves, breast, comfortably, courage","count":46,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H7307","lemma":"רוּחַ","xlit":"rûwach","gloss":"wind","kjv":"air, anger, blast, breath","count":14,"share":0.05},{"strong":"H974","lemma":"בָּחַן","xlit":"bâchan","gloss":"to test","kjv":"examine, prove, tempt, try","count":8,"share":0.03},{"strong":"H3559","lemma":"כּוּן","xlit":"kûwn","gloss":"to be erect","kjv":"certain, confirm, direct, faithfulness","count":11,"share":0.04},{"strong":"H995","lemma":"בִּין","xlit":"bîyn","gloss":"to separate mentally","kjv":"attend, consider, be cunning, diligently","count":10,"share":0.04}],"verses